{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.RoughMeanGradient.actual_rough_mean_gradient",
      "title": "The actual PBPS conditional mean gradient on all of L2",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
          "label": "Fixed PBPS2609.06905v1 C.1 density/closedness passage and C.2 sharp compact estimate toward B.13; actual rough-input conditional mean in the SAME canonical closed-gradient graph and sharp energy estimate. Source C2/two Hessian/positive capped eta retained.",
          "scope": "One genuine dense closable compact-gradient G, one bounded actual conditional mean T and one bounded vector-L2 gradient K are chosen before all rough L2(ν) inputs. (Tu,Ku) lies in the actual closed compact-gradient graph; the sharp c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)] norm defect and source4η bound hold. Original C2/two Hessian bounds/positive capped step retained. Finite Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicitly extends source Euclidean setting. Every-y literal kernel law is distinct from AE rough mean/fiber L1 and squareL1. Separately defined weak-H1 equivalence, full B13/Gamma/dynamics/main/error/cost/composition remain open."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSRoughMeanGradient"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite real Hilbert/Borel E and canonical volume; rank zero explicitly extends the source Euclidean presentation.",
        "V is C2, α>0, α≤β, both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
        "Every u is an arbitrary real square-integrable AE class under actual ν. No centering, compact support, extra moment, pointwise smoothness or caller normalization/operator/domain/convergence premise.",
        "One G,T,K produced uniformly before u; only AE ν rough mean/fiber integrability. Ḡ is the closure of the exact compact-gradient graph, with no unstated weak-Sobolev convention."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd and EVERY-y S_y=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)). Then ν is a probability. There is a densely defined closable real linear gradient G:L²(ν)⇀L²(ν;E), whose graph consists exactly of AE classes (φ,∇φ) for smooth compactly supported φ, and whose closure has closed graph. There are one bounded linear T:L²(ν)→L²(ν) and one bounded linear K:L²(ν)→L²(ν;E), both chosen before all arbitrary rough u∈L²(ν). For every u, (Tu,Ku)∈graph(Ḡ), ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S_y(dx) AE ν, and u,u² are integrable under S_y for AE y. With c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)], η‖Ku‖²≤c(‖u‖²−‖Tu‖²) and 4η‖Ku‖²≤‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². No compactness, centering, extra moment, supplied kernel/operator/domain or convergence certificate is assumed for rough u. This is the closed compact-gradient formulation of the source density/closedness passage and sharp estimate; a separately defined weak-H1 equivalence and full Gamma/B13 identity are not claimed.",
      "formula": "\\forall u\\in L^2(\\nu):\\quad(Tu,Ku)\\in\\operatorname{graph}(\\overline G),\\quad Tu(y)=\\int u(x)S_y(dx)\\ (\\nu\\text{-a.e.}),\\quad\\eta\\|Ku\\|^2\\le\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}\\bigl(\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2\\bigr),\\quad4\\eta\\|Ku\\|^2\\le\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2.",
      "boundary": "One genuine dense closable compact-gradient G, one bounded actual conditional mean T and one bounded vector-L2 gradient K are chosen before all rough L2(ν) inputs. (Tu,Ku) lies in the actual closed compact-gradient graph; the sharp c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)] norm defect and source4η bound hold. Original C2/two Hessian bounds/positive capped step retained. Finite Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicitly extends source Euclidean setting. Every-y literal kernel law is distinct from AE rough mean/fiber L1 and squareL1. Separately defined weak-H1 equivalence, full B13/Gamma/dynamics/main/error/cost/composition remain open.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Use the actual source laws, dense core and bounded mean",
          "text": "The three admitted parents supply the same μ,J,ν: the actual all-L2 source mean T and contraction; a genuine dense closable compact-gradient core G with closed graph closure; and the sharp compact gradient energy. The actual conditional S is stationary under ν because it disintegrates the reflected joint law Λ and both Λ marginals are ν. Thus u=φ AE ν also holds AE S_y for AE y. This fiber fact is derived from the actual stationary law, not assumed by a caller.",
          "formula": "\\nu=J_2,\\quad\\Lambda_1=\\Lambda_2=\\nu,\\quad S\\circ\\nu=\\nu,\\quad\\overline{\\operatorname{dom}G}=L^2(\\nu);\\qquad u=\\varphi\\ (\\nu\\text{-a.e.})\\Rightarrow u=\\varphi\\ (S_y\\text{-a.e.},\\ \\nu\\text{-a.e. }y).",
          "lean": "L2MacroscopicMean.actual_macroscopic_l2_mean; SourceMeanGradientDomain.literal_source_mean_in_closed_gradient; MacroscopicEnergy.actual_macroscopic_gradient_energy_blocks; Measure.disintegrate; Measure.ae_ae_of_ae_comp"
        },
        {
          "title": "Match compact representatives and the sharp energy on the same law",
          "text": "For u in domG take its genuine smooth compact representative φ. The compact parent produces Tf(y)=∫φ dS_y and an actual pair ([Tf],[∇Tf]) in graphḠ; Tf need not be compactly supported. The fiber equality, exact every-y kernel tilt, and AE uniqueness identify Tu=[Tf]. The actual macroscopic energy parent supplies η∫‖∇Tf‖²dν≤c‖Bg‖² for g=φ∘snd, and the real block identity gives ‖Bg‖²=∫φ²dν−∫(Tf)²dν. Canonical L2 norm/integral identities match these exact classes.",
          "formula": "Tu=[T\\varphi],\\quad(Tu,v)\\in\\operatorname{graph}(\\overline G),\\quad\\eta\\|v\\|^2\\le c(\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2),\\qquad c=\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}.",
          "lean": "hCore; hTu; hSame; hUn; hTn′; hGradn; hBlock₁; L2.inner_def; integral_congr_ae"
        },
        {
          "title": "Construct a genuine linear derivative on the dense core",
          "text": "The previous step proves Tu belongs to domḠ for every core u. Restrict T to that domain and compose with the actual partial linear map Ḡ: Du=Ḡ(Tu). This is a real linear map on domG. Single-valued graph uniqueness identifies Du with the compact derivative witness, so it retains the sharp estimate. Linearity is derived through the genuine gradient graph, not chosen separately for each observer.",
          "formula": "D:\\operatorname{dom}G\\to L^2(\\nu;E),\\quad Du=\\overline G(Tu),\\quad(Tu,Du)\\in\\operatorname{graph}(\\overline G),\\quad\\eta\\|Du\\|^2\\le c(\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2).",
          "lean": "hDom; q; LinearMap.codRestrict; G.closure.toFun.comp; hDpair; LinearPMap.mem_graph_snd_inj; hDsharp"
        },
        {
          "title": "Extend the bounded derivative and preserve graph and sharp defect",
          "text": "Since c≥0 and η>0, the sharp core estimate implies ‖Du‖≤√(c/η)‖u‖. The actual inclusion domG→L²(ν) has dense range; vector L2 is complete. Mathlib extendOfNorm therefore constructs one bounded linear K on full L2 agreeing with D on the core. The preimage of closed graphḠ under u↦(Tu,Ku) is closed, and so is the sharp-inequality set. Density extends both to every rough u. This uses the repaired source prerequisite path core gradient→linear norm bound→bounded extension; no limit or closed-domain premise is imported.",
          "formula": "\\|Du\\|\\le\\sqrt{c/\\eta}\\|u\\|,\\quad K|_{\\operatorname{dom}G}=D;\\qquad\\forall u\\in L^2(\\nu):\\ (Tu,Ku)\\in\\operatorname{graph}(\\overline G),\\quad\\eta\\|Ku\\|^2\\le c(\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2).",
          "lean": "hNormBound; hRange; LinearMap.extendOfNorm; LinearMap.extendOfNorm_eq; hPairAll; hSharpAll; Dense.induction; isClosed_le"
        },
        {
          "title": "Recover the source coefficient without a singular endpoint division",
          "text": "The original α≤β and βη≤1 give 0≤αη≤1. Hence 0≤c≤1/4. Since T is contractive, Δ=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖²≥0, and η‖Ku‖²≤cΔ≤Δ/4. The literal AE source mean and AE fiber L1/squareL1 are retained from the true all-L2 mean producer. The proof never divides by 1−αη, so the allowed αη=1 endpoint is included.",
          "formula": "0\\le\\alpha\\eta\\le1,\\quad0\\le c\\le\\tfrac14,\\quad\\Delta_u=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2\\ge0,\\quad\\eta\\|Ku\\|^2\\le c\\Delta_u\\le\\tfrac14\\Delta_u.",
          "lean": "haη; haη1; hcCap; hNonneg; hSharpAll; hAll; hSd"
        },
        {
          "title": "Exercise the actual joint block and the allowed endpoint",
          "text": "The genuine joint-space Test obtains actual U,M and B=(I−P)UP from the same source mean parent. AE uniqueness of both literal source conditional means identifies the T from this theorem with that parent T. For arbitrary rough u−v, the parent defect and linearity give η‖Ku−Kv‖²≤c‖BM(u−v)‖² and the source4η version; PM(u−v)=M(u−v) and M(Tu−Tv)=PUPM(u−v). A separate endpoint Test uses αη=1 to force the full bounded gradient operator K=0 and retains (Tu,0) in the same closed graph. The endpoint equality is a Test specialization, not an added public theorem premise.",
          "formula": "\\eta\\|Ku-Kv\\|^2\\le c\\|BM(u-v)\\|^2,\\quad4\\eta\\|Ku-Kv\\|^2\\le\\|BM(u-v)\\|^2;\\qquad\\alpha\\eta=1\\Rightarrow K=0,\\ (Tu,0)\\in\\operatorname{graph}(\\overline G).",
          "lean": "Tests.ProximalBPSRoughMeanGradient.actual_joint_block_rough_difference; actual_sharp_endpoint_zero_gradient"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ and Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd and EVERY-y S_y=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)). Then ν is a probability. There is a densely defined closable real linear gradient G:L²(ν)⇀L²(ν;E), whose graph consists exactly of AE classes (φ,∇φ) for smooth compactly supported φ, and whose closure has closed graph. There are one bounded linear T:L²(ν)→L²(ν) and one bounded linear K:L²(ν)→L²(ν;E), both chosen before all arbitrary rough u∈L²(ν). For every u, (Tu,Ku)∈graph(Ḡ), ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S_y(dx) AE ν, and u,u² are integrable under S_y for AE y. With c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)], η‖Ku‖²≤c(‖u‖²−‖Tu‖²) and 4η‖Ku‖²≤‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². No compactness, centering, extra moment, supplied kernel/operator/domain or convergence certificate is assumed for rough u. This is the closed compact-gradient formulation of the source density/closedness passage and sharp estimate; a separately defined weak-H1 equivalence and full Gamma/B13 identity are not claimed.",
      "lean_proof": "Use the actual source laws, dense core and bounded mean; Match compact representatives and the sharp energy on the same law; Construct a genuine linear derivative on the dense core; Extend the bounded derivative and preserve graph and sharp defect; Recover the source coefficient without a singular endpoint division; Exercise the actual joint block and the allowed endpoint",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.SourceMeanGradientDomain.literal_source_mean_in_closed_gradient",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.L2MacroscopicMean.actual_macroscopic_l2_mean",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.MacroscopicEnergy.actual_macroscopic_gradient_energy_blocks"
      ],
      "mathlib_dependencies": [
        "Measure.disintegrate",
        "Measure.ae_ae_of_ae_comp",
        "Lp.ext",
        "L2.inner_def",
        "LinearMap.codRestrict",
        "LinearPMap.mem_graph_snd_inj",
        "LinearMap.extendOfNorm",
        "LinearMap.extendOfNorm_eq",
        "Dense.induction",
        "isClosed_le"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
